{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And you shall know that</b> — dwelling in Zion, and strangers shall not pass through it anymore — if they keep the Torah of HaShem. Thus are the words of Zechariah: \"and I shall dwell in your midst.\" And thus he says at the end: \"And it shall be, if you hearken to the voice of YHWH\" — then all this shall be fulfilled."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The Hebrew text quotes Joel 4:17 in the lemma but is written as a single run; I have divided the bolded lemma from the comment. The Zechariah citation is partial (cf. Zechariah 2:14); the closing quotation appears to paraphrase a conditional promise resembling Deuteronomy 28:1."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:52.814891952Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}